  "findings": [
    {
      "rubric_id": "R1",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "section 2.7 join table; P1a runs-watch.js scope file names and lock name; P1c register.ts scope derivation; scripts/session-mode.js marker",
      "claim": "The plan uses project_key as the join segment in every file name (runs/<project_key>.lock, runs/<project_key>--<root_run_id>.json, review/<project_key>.index.lock, ~/.autopilot/review/<project_key>/) but never defines how project_key is derived from repo_identity, and the mod cannot derive it at all: P1c says scope is inferred from the session-mode marker's repo_root plus AUTOPILOT_ROOT_RUN_ID, yet repo_identity is git-common-dir:<realpath>, which requires running git (forbidden by section 2.5: no process spawn, no Node, no repo lib) and which differs from repo_root in a linked worktree. Env var access from the mod sandbox is also not among the verified API surfaces.",
      "evidence": "Section 2.5 defines project = repo_identity = git-common-dir:<realpath> and forbids $.process in the mod. Section 2.7 lists repo_identity as the canonical key but no project_key row. P1a names files by <project_key> and uses '--' as a scope separator without stating that the key cannot contain '--' or path characters (repo_identity contains ':' and '/'). P1c: 'scope 由 ~/.autopilot/session-mode/<sid>.json 的 repo_root + AUTOPILOT_ROOT_RUN_ID 推'. No step writes repo_identity or root_run_id into the marker.",
      "evidence_reference": "plan sections 2.5 (身分), 2.7, 3 (file map rows for runs-watch.js and session-mode.js), 4 P1a watcher paragraph, 4 P1c register.ts bullet",
      "repair": "Add a project_key row to section 2.7: project_key = a fixed, filesystem-safe digest of repo_identity (for example first 16 hex of sha256) computed by one shared function in scripts/lib (used by runs-watch.js, render-review-page.js, session-mode.js, portfolio-replan.js). Have scripts/session-mode.js set write repo_identity, project_key, root_run_id (from AUTOPILOT_ROOT_RUN_ID) and session_id into the marker, and specify that the mod reads only the marker (via $.fs.read) and never computes identity or reads env. Extend S2 to read the marker from both terminal and desktop.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": true,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": true,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": true,
      "provenance": [
        {
          "seat_id": "claude_architecture",
          "runner": "claude-native",
          "model": "claude-fable-5-1"
        }
      ],
      "duplicate_reports": [],
      "disposition": null,
      "fingerprint": "571c60e4d5027832b427bd723f2e597f3a5402877d1309722c5ef4ad1ae20205"
    },
    {
      "rubric_id": "R2",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "scripts/dispatch-hetero.sh, scripts/dispatch-review.sh, scripts/dispatch-author.sh manifest field repo_identity; hooks/tests/manifest-repo-identity.test.sh",
      "claim": "The shell derivation of repo_identity is underspecified and the named test does not pin parity with repoIdentity(): the file map says the value is computed from CONSUMING_REPO_ROOT / REPO_ROOT without stating precedence or whether all three scripts export both, and git rev-parse --git-common-dir returns a relative '.git' in a main worktree but an absolute path in a linked worktree, so a shell port that does not realpath the result relative to that root will produce a different string from the Node implementation and every --project filter will silently miss.",
      "evidence": "Section 3 row: 'manifest 加 repo_identity（由 CONSUMING_REPO_ROOT／REPO_ROOT 算 git-common-dir:<realpath>）'. P1a: 'manifest-repo-identity.test.sh 斷言三種 role 都寫、舊 manifest 缺欄不炸' — no assertion that the written value equals repoIdentity(root) for a main checkout and a linked worktree, and no assertion for the case where CONSUMING_REPO_ROOT differs from REPO_ROOT. The cited task-runtime.js L36–46 is not present in this review checkout, so the exact normalisation it performs could not be compared.",
      "evidence_reference": "plan section 3 (dispatch-*.sh row), section 4 P1a second bullet, section 2.6 compatibility impact",
      "repair": "State the rule once in section 2.5 or 2.7: root = CONSUMING_REPO_ROOT if set, else REPO_ROOT; value = 'git-common-dir:' + realpath(git -C root rev-parse --git-common-dir resolved against root). Make manifest-repo-identity.test.sh assert, for each of the three roles, that the manifest value byte-equals node -e output of repoIdentity(root) in (a) a main checkout, (b) a git worktree add linked checkout, (c) CONSUMING_REPO_ROOT pointing at a different repo than REPO_ROOT. Also confirm no manifest JSON schema with additionalProperties false exists under schemas/ (not listed in the file map) before adding the field.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": true,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": true,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": true,
      "provenance": [
        {
          "seat_id": "claude_architecture",
          "runner": "claude-native",
          "model": "claude-fable-5-1"
        }
      ],
      "duplicate_reports": [],
      "disposition": null,
      "fingerprint": "5b205f5d4681010769a57a18583f46a70291aa6da34b1e945cc02c3440c97f53"
    },
    {
      "rubric_id": "R5",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "src/status/runs-watch.js writer lock; scripts/render-review-page.js index lock; scripts/session-mode.js set; --stop pid verification",
      "claim": "The single-writer guarantee and the crash-recovery property both rest on flock semantics (lock released when the fd closes), but section 2.5 restricts implementation to Node built-ins, and Node has no flock. A plain lockfile does not release on crash, which would break the R-A04 recovery story (next session-mode set re-acquires after a crash). The plan also says --stop verifies the lock holder pid, but flock exposes no holder query.",
      "evidence": "Section 2.5: 'Node ≥ 20.10，只用 built-ins'. P1a: 'flock -n <live-base>/runs/<project_key>.lock'; lifecycle: 'crash：lock 由 OS 釋放'; '--stop（核對 lock 持有者 pid 後送 SIGTERM）'. P1b: 'flock project 級 <live-base>/review/<project_key>.index.lock（手動跑 renderer 也要拿）'. No mechanism named for either lock that is reachable from Node built-ins.",
      "evidence_reference": "plan sections 2.5 (Node built-ins), 4 P1a watcher and lifecycle paragraphs, 4 P1b 發佈 paragraph, section 6 row 'watcher 死了沒人重起'",
      "repair": "Decide the mechanism explicitly: either (a) session-mode.js and the manual --watch path launch the watcher as flock -n <lock> node src/status/runs-watch.js ... (util-linux flock(1), documented as a platform dependency under section 2.6 like python3), with runs-watch.js writing writer.pid into the envelope immediately after start so --stop reads the pid from the envelope and signals it; or (b) runs-watch.js self-re-execs under flock(1) when not already wrapped. Apply the same choice to the index lock in render-review-page.js. Add a negative control: kill -9 the watcher, assert flock -n on the lock succeeds within one tick.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": true,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": true,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": true,
      "provenance": [
        {
          "seat_id": "claude_architecture",
          "runner": "claude-native",
          "model": "claude-fable-5-1"
        }
      ],
      "duplicate_reports": [],
      "disposition": null,
      "fingerprint": "0a671af5e9650f8b9dc0ab6b46484e14b87f1acdc8531342f8092c1c9a9d5bb7"
    },
    {
      "rubric_id": "R5",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "non-blocking",
      "affected_surface": "scripts/render-review-page.js job publish (v-<ts>/ and current symlink); watcher --render vs manual renderer",
      "claim": "The index publish is serialised by the project index lock, but the per-job current pointer switch is not: the watcher's debounced --render and a manual render-review-page.js run on the same job can each build a v-<ts>/ and rename current, and the slower process may win with an older published_at, leaving current pointing at the older version. The plan names only the index lock.",
      "evidence": "P1b: '手動 render-review-page.js 同一路徑'; publish steps describe tmp symlink then rename(current.tmp, current) with no job-level lock and no monotonic check against the current target; the project index.lock is described as covering index.html only.",
      "evidence_reference": "plan section 4 P1b 發佈 and 觸發 paragraphs",
      "repair": "Hold the project index lock for the whole job publish (build, smoke, switch, index update) rather than only the index step, or before the rename compare the target of current with the new v-<ts> and skip the switch if the existing target is newer. Add this as a fourth publish scenario in render-review-page.test.sh.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": false,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": false,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": false,
      "provenance": [
