      "claim": "The single-writer design is substantially correct (project-level flock watcher, scope-split files, reader scope verification, separate index.lock also taken by the manual renderer, tmp→rename symlink switch with three failure-scenario tests), but the plan does not name one residual window it otherwise promises to name: a reader that resolved the old version directory just before the symlink switch can still be reading a version directory that the retention rule deletes in the same publish cycle (keep one previous version, delete older), i.e. an open-page refresh vs. reap race between deletion and the reader's next fetch.",
